---
import ComingSoon from '../layouts/ComingSoon.astro';
---

<ComingSoon title="The Compliance Layer for AI-Generated Code">

<!-- Hero -->
<section class="hero">
  <div class="container hero-inner">
    <div class="hero-badge">Early Access</div>
    <h1>Stop auditing AI code<br /><span class="gradient-text">by hand</span></h1>
    <p class="hero-sub">
      Sentrik scans every commit against 24 regulatory and security frameworks, blocks non-compliant code in CI, and generates audit evidence automatically. Works in VS Code, Cursor, and CI/CD pipelines &mdash; one tool, zero config.
    </p>
    <div class="hero-actions">
      <a href="#get-free" class="btn btn-primary btn-lg">Get Early Access</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- The Problem -->
<section class="problem">
  <div class="container">
    <h2 class="section-title">The Problem</h2>
    <p class="section-sub">AI writes code faster than humans can review it. Compliance can't keep up.</p>
    <div class="problem-grid">
      <div class="problem-card">
        <div class="problem-stat">$3B</div>
        <p>fine for TD Bank in 2024 &mdash; 70,000 unreviewed compliance alerts. Manual review doesn&rsquo;t scale <a href="https://www.reuters.com/business/finance/td-bank-pays-3-billion-fine-us-money-laundering-failures-2024-10-10/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="stat-cite">[Reuters]</a></p>
      </div>
      <div class="problem-card">
        <div class="problem-stat">$40B/yr</div>
        <p>spent on compliance labor in the US alone &mdash; 400,000 workers &mdash; and outcomes are still failing <a href="https://a16z.com/everything-everywhere-is-compliance/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="stat-cite">[a16z]</a></p>
      </div>
      <div class="problem-card">
        <div class="problem-stat">36%</div>
        <p>of AI-generated code contains security vulnerabilities <a href="https://www.theregister.com/2025/01/24/ai_code_security/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="stat-cite">[The Register]</a></p>
      </div>
      <div class="problem-card">
        <div class="problem-stat">595</div>
        <p>rules across 24 regulatory and security frameworks, ready out of the box</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- The Governance Gap -->
<section class="narrative-gap">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="narrative-inner">
      <h2>The assumption that broke compliance</h2>
      <p class="narrative-lead">Every compliance framework, every audit process, every security review was designed around one thing: <em>a human touched every line of code.</em></p>
      <p>That assumption is now false for most teams. AI coding assistants write an ever-growing share of production code &mdash; on some teams the majority. Developers review at high speed under pressure to merge fast. A developer staring at 400 lines of AI-generated code doesn&rsquo;t know whether it violates HIPAA clause 164.312 or IEC 62304 section 5.5.3 &mdash; and doesn&rsquo;t have time to find out.</p>
      <p>The result: organizations are running compliance risk they can&rsquo;t see. Not because they&rsquo;re negligent, but because the tools they have weren&rsquo;t designed for this world. Semgrep, Snyk, SonarQube &mdash; they scan for issues. They don&rsquo;t govern AI agents. They don&rsquo;t know that Claude Code wrote the code, that the agent declared a scope of <code>app/db/**</code>, that it actually touched <code>app/auth/login.py</code>, and that this is a scope violation that should be surfaced immediately and logged permanently.</p>
      <div class="narrative-callout">
        <strong>Sentrik is the governance layer built for this world.</strong> The AI writes the code. Sentrik enforces the rules, catches violations in real time, and generates the cryptographically signed audit evidence &mdash; automatically, at every commit, without slowing anyone down.
      </div>
      <blockquote class="narrative-quote">
        &ldquo;For the first time, the risk of an enterprise <em>not</em> modernizing its compliance stack outweighs the risk of change.&rdquo;
        <cite>&mdash; Andreessen Horowitz, <a href="https://a16z.com/everything-everywhere-is-compliance/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Everything, Everywhere is Compliance</a> (May 2026)</cite>
      </blockquote>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- How It Works -->
<section class="how-it-works">
  <div class="container">
    <h2 class="section-title">Three Commands. Full Compliance.</h2>
    <div class="steps-grid">
      <div class="step-card">
        <div class="step-num">1</div>
        <h3>Scan</h3>
        <code class="step-cmd">sentrik scan</code>
        <p>595 rules check your code against IEC 62304, HIPAA, SOC2, OWASP, GDPR, EU AI Act, NIST 800-53, and 17 more frameworks. Findings map to specific regulatory clauses.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="step-card">
        <div class="step-num">2</div>
        <h3>Gate</h3>
        <code class="step-cmd">sentrik gate</code>
        <p>Block non-compliant code in CI. PR comments show exactly which regulation you're violating.</p>
        <pre class="step-yaml"><code>- name: Compliance Gate
  run: sentrik gate
    --git-range origin/main...HEAD
    --decorate-pr</code></pre>
      </div>
      <div class="step-card">
        <div class="step-num">3</div>
        <h3>Ship</h3>
        <code class="step-cmd">sentrik attest</code>
        <p>Generate cryptographically signed attestations, per-framework compliance reports, and audit-ready evidence bundles. No more 6-week evidence sprints.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- The Scenario -->
<section class="scenario-section">
  <div class="container">
    <h2 class="section-title">Two agents. One project. One that stays in bounds.</h2>
    <p class="section-sub">This is what AI governance looks like in practice &mdash; not a policy document, but a live enforcement layer that catches problems before they reach main.</p>
    <div class="scenario-grid">
      <div class="scenario-agent clean">
        <div class="scenario-status pass">Gate Passed</div>
        <h3>Agent 1 &mdash; Fix SQL Injection</h3>
        <code class="scenario-cmd">sentrik task-bind "Fix SQL injection in patient endpoint" --path "app/routes/patients.py" "app/db/**"</code>
        <p>Agent declares its intent and authorized file scope. Works within <code>app/db/**</code>. Query parameterized. Gate passes. A signed attestation is generated: <em>&ldquo;IEC 62304 &sect;5.5.3 evaluated. SQL injection finding remediated at commit c28a5d.&rdquo;</em></p>
      </div>
      <div class="scenario-agent rogue">
        <div class="scenario-status fail">Gate Blocked</div>
        <h3>Agent 2 &mdash; Patch Logging Module</h3>
        <code class="scenario-cmd">sentrik task-bind "Patch logging module" --path "app/logging/**"</code>
        <p>Agent declares scope: <code>app/logging/**</code>. Actually touches <code>app/auth/login.py</code>, <code>app/billing/invoice.py</code>, <code>app/secrets/keys.py</code>, and six more files. Sentrik catches it the moment it writes outside its declared scope.</p>
        <div class="scenario-alert">Anomaly score: 0.92 &nbsp;&bull;&nbsp; Status: VIOLATED<br/>9 unauthorized files &nbsp;&bull;&nbsp; New zones: auth, billing, crypto, secrets<br/>Gate blocked &nbsp;&bull;&nbsp; Rollback available &nbsp;&bull;&nbsp; Signed incident record created</div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="scenario-footer">The security lead sees the violation in the dashboard, reviews the exact out-of-scope files, rolls back with one click, and creates a work item for investigation &mdash; all before any unauthorized code reaches main. The entire incident is logged in a signed, tamper-evident audit record. This is what human-in-the-loop AI governance actually looks like.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- Terminal Demo -->
<section class="demo">
  <div class="container">
    <h2 class="section-title">See It In Action</h2>
    <div class="terminal">
      <div class="terminal-header">
        <span class="terminal-dot red"></span>
        <span class="terminal-dot yellow"></span>
        <span class="terminal-dot green"></span>
        <span class="terminal-title">sentrik</span>
      </div>
      <div class="terminal-body">
        <div id="main-player"></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="demo-tabs">
      <button class="demo-tab active" data-cast="/recordings/05-full-lifecycle.cast">Full Lifecycle</button>
      <button class="demo-tab" data-cast="/recordings/01-init-and-scan.cast">Scan &amp; Findings</button>
      <button class="demo-tab" data-cast="/recordings/02-fix-and-gate.cast">Fix &amp; Gate</button>
      <button class="demo-tab" data-cast="/recordings/03-supply-chain.cast">Supply Chain</button>
      <button class="demo-tab" data-cast="/recordings/04-compliance.cast">Reports</button>
      <span class="demo-tab-divider"></span>
      <button class="demo-tab" data-cast="/recordings/quality-score.cast">Quality Score</button>
      <button class="demo-tab" data-cast="/recordings/project-profile.cast">Project Profile</button>
      <button class="demo-tab" data-cast="/recordings/design-review.cast">Design Review</button>
      <button class="demo-tab" data-cast="/recordings/expertise.cast">Expertise Check</button>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- Mid-page CTA -->
<section class="mid-cta">
  <div class="container" style="text-align:center">
    <a href="#get-free" class="btn btn-primary btn-lg">Get Early Access</a>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- AI Governance Philosophy -->
<section class="philosophy-section">
  <div class="container">
    <h2 class="section-title">Your AI Agents Fly.<br /><span class="gradient-text">You Stay in Command.</span></h2>
    <p class="section-sub">AI coding agents write the code. Sentrik monitors every move, enforces your compliance boundaries, and produces the signed audit record &mdash; without slowing the agents down.</p>
    <div class="philosophy-pillars">
      <div class="philosophy-pillar">
        <div class="philosophy-icon">
          <svg width="28" height="28" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="3"/><path d="M12 1v3M12 20v3M4.22 4.22l2.12 2.12M17.66 17.66l2.12 2.12M1 12h3M20 12h3M4.22 19.78l2.12-2.12M17.66 6.34l2.12-2.12"/></svg>
        </div>
        <h3>Monitor</h3>
        <p>Every file touched, every rule evaluated, every agent action logged in a tamper-evident audit trail &mdash; in real time.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="philosophy-pillar">
        <div class="philosophy-icon">
          <svg width="28" height="28" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M12 22s8-4 8-10V5l-8-3-8 3v7c0 6 8 10 8 10z"/></svg>
        </div>
        <h3>Enforce</h3>
        <p>Gate boundaries are set by your team, not the AI. Non-compliant code is blocked before it reaches main &mdash; automatically.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="philosophy-pillar">
        <div class="philosophy-icon">
          <svg width="28" height="28" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M9 12l2 2 4-4"/><path d="M12 2l2.09 2.09L17 3l1 2.83L21 7l-1.17 2.83L21 13l-2.83 1L17 17l-2.83-.83L12 18l-2.09-2.09L7 17l-1-2.83L3 13l1.17-2.83L3 7l2.83-1L7 3z"/></svg>
        </div>
        <h3>Certify</h3>
        <p>Cryptographically signed attestations and per-framework evidence bundles, generated at every commit. Audit-ready on demand.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- Who It's For -->
<section class="audience-section">
  <div class="container">
    <h2 class="section-title">One platform. Every stakeholder.</h2>
    <p class="section-sub">Different people. Different problems. One governance layer that connects them all.</p>
    <div class="audience-grid">
      <div class="audience-card">
        <div class="audience-role">Developer</div>
        <h3>Compliance as a fast feedback loop, not a blocker</h3>
        <p>Findings appear inline in VS Code before you push. AI agents check compliance during code generation via MCP &mdash; so generated code passes the gate on the first try. The gate rarely blocks because it already ran during development.</p>
        <div class="audience-quote">&ldquo;My first commit is already compliant.&rdquo;</div>
      </div>
      <div class="audience-card">
        <div class="audience-role">Engineering Manager</div>
        <h3>Structural guarantees instead of manual oversight</h3>
        <p>Non-compliant code structurally cannot merge without a human decision. Scope violations are caught the moment they happen &mdash; not in a post-mortem. Work item traceability maps findings to sprints so compliance has a home in your process.</p>
        <div class="audience-quote">&ldquo;The gate is always on. I don&rsquo;t have to remember to check.&rdquo;</div>
      </div>
      <div class="audience-card">
        <div class="audience-role">CISO / Security Lead</div>
        <h3>A signed audit trail for every AI action</h3>
        <p>Cryptographically signed attestations at every commit. Human-in-the-loop approvals for every gated action. Every agent session tracked &mdash; what it intended, what it touched, whether it stayed in scope, and what happened when it didn&rsquo;t.</p>
        <div class="audience-quote">&ldquo;When the auditor asks, I have the evidence ready.&rdquo;</div>
      </div>
      <div class="audience-card">
        <div class="audience-role">Compliance Officer / Auditor</div>
        <h3>Positive evidence of compliance &mdash; not just a list of violations</h3>
        <p>The Evidence Map shows where in the code each regulatory requirement is satisfied &mdash; with file, line, and matched pattern. Per-framework compliance reports generated in seconds. Audit prep is a download, not a sprint.</p>
        <div class="audience-quote">&ldquo;Six weeks of evidence gathering became a five-minute export.&rdquo;</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- The Regulatory Window -->
<section class="regulatory-window">
  <div class="container">
    <h2 class="section-title">The regulatory window is closing</h2>
    <p class="section-sub">Regulators are catching up to AI development. Organizations that establish governance now will have processes and evidence in place before enforcement begins &mdash; those that don&rsquo;t will scramble to reconstruct it.</p>
    <div class="regulatory-grid">
      <div class="regulatory-item">
        <div class="reg-status active">Transparency Rules: Aug 2026</div>
        <h3>EU AI Act</h3>
        <p>Article 50 transparency obligations and enforcement powers land August 2, 2026; high-risk system obligations follow December 2, 2027 (Annex III). The required evidence covers how systems are built between now and then. Non-compliance carries fines up to 3% of global revenue for high-risk obligations.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="regulatory-item">
        <div class="reg-status active">Active &amp; Escalating</div>
        <h3>HIPAA Enforcement</h3>
        <p>Healthcare compliance frameworks are increasingly scrutinizing how AI-generated code is governed in systems that handle ePHI. &ldquo;We review it manually&rdquo; is not a scalable answer when AI generates thousands of lines daily.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="regulatory-item">
        <div class="reg-status active">FDA Guidance Issued</div>
        <h3>FDA / IEC 62304</h3>
        <p>21 CFR Part 11 and IEC 62304 compliance must be demonstrated across the full development lifecycle &mdash; including AI-assisted code generation. The evidence requirement doesn&rsquo;t stop at the output.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="regulatory-item">
        <div class="reg-status emerging">Questions Now Standard</div>
        <h3>SOC 2 &amp; NIST AI RMF</h3>
        <p>SOC 2 auditors are adding AI governance questions to standard assessments. NIST AI RMF requires organizations to demonstrate governance of AI systems. &ldquo;How do you govern AI-generated code?&rdquo; needs a real answer.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- Dashboard & AI -->
<section class="dashboard-section">
  <div class="container">
    <h2 class="section-title">A Compliance Dashboard That Actually Helps</h2>
    <p class="section-sub">Real-time compliance scores, findings browser, AI-powered fixes, and one-click audit evidence &mdash; all in the browser.</p>

    <div class="showcase-block">
      <div class="showcase-text">
        <h3>Compliance Overview</h3>
        <p>See your compliance score, finding counts by severity, gate status, and scan duration at a glance. Governance banners flag when human review is required before merge.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="showcase-img">
        <img src="/images/dashboard-overview.png" alt="Sentrik dashboard showing compliance score, findings summary, and gate status" class="screenshot expandable" loading="lazy" />
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="showcase-block reverse">
      <div class="showcase-text">
        <h3>AI Agent Governance</h3>
        <p>Sentrik auto-detects AI agents (Claude Code, Cursor, Copilot) and enforces declared task scope. When an agent touches files outside its declared intent, the violation is flagged immediately &mdash; with the full list of unauthorized files, rollback controls, and a pending approval that blocks the gate until a human signs off.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="showcase-img">
        <img src="/images/ai-activity-dashboard.png" alt="AI Activity dashboard showing a scope violation from Claude Code touching 8 unauthorized files, with rollback and approval controls" class="screenshot expandable" loading="lazy" />
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="showcase-block">
      <div class="showcase-text">
        <h3>Compliance Evidence Map</h3>
        <p>Most tools only show what's <em>wrong</em>. Sentrik also shows what's <em>right</em>. The Evidence Map pinpoints exactly where your code satisfies each regulatory requirement &mdash; with file, line number, and matched pattern. Auditors see proof of compliance, not just a list of violations.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="showcase-img">
        <img src="/images/evidence-map-dashboard.png" alt="Compliance Evidence Map showing 87.2% coverage across HIPAA, OWASP, SOC 2 with code-level evidence" class="screenshot expandable" loading="lazy" />
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="showcase-block">
      <div class="showcase-text">
        <h3>Findings with Code Context</h3>
        <p>Every finding shows the exact file, line number, regulatory clause, and code snippet. Filter by severity, rule, or framework. Export to CSV for auditors.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="showcase-img">
        <img src="/images/finding-detail.png" alt="Finding detail view showing code snippet with compliance violation highlighted" class="screenshot expandable" loading="lazy" />
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="showcase-block">
      <div class="showcase-text">
        <h3>Requirement Drift Detection</h3>
        <p>Sentrik compares your code against documented requirements and flags when they diverge. When drift is detected, work items are automatically created in GitHub Issues, Azure DevOps, or Jira &mdash; assigned, labeled, and linked to the finding. No manual triage.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="showcase-img">
        <img src="/images/dash-work-items.png" alt="Work items automatically created from requirement drift findings" class="screenshot expandable" loading="lazy" />
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="showcase-block reverse">
      <div class="showcase-text">
        <h3>Fix with AI</h3>
        <p>Click any finding, chat with an LLM, and apply the fix &mdash; all from the browser. Compliance officers triage findings without touching an IDE.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="showcase-img">
        <img src="/images/ai-chat-panel.png" alt="AI chat panel explaining how to fix a compliance finding" class="screenshot expandable" loading="lazy" />
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="showcase-block">
      <div class="showcase-text">
        <h3>STRIDE Threat Modeling</h3>
        <p>An LLM analyses your code for spoofing, tampering, repudiation, information disclosure, denial of service, and elevation of privilege threats. Filter by STRIDE category or severity, discuss mitigations with AI, and track remediation status.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="showcase-img">
        <img src="/images/threat-model-chat.png" alt="Threat model dashboard with AI chat panel open discussing mitigation strategies" class="screenshot expandable" loading="lazy" />
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="showcase-block reverse">
      <div class="showcase-text">
        <h3>AI-Assisted Code Generation</h3>
        <p>Claude Code, Cursor, and VS Code call Sentrik via MCP. The AI checks compliance rules <em>before</em> writing code &mdash; so generated code passes the gate on the first try. The VS Code extension scans on every save with inline diagnostics.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="showcase-img">
        <img src="/images/mcp-in-action.png" alt="AI agent checking compliance rules during code generation" class="screenshot expandable" loading="lazy" />
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- Code Intelligence -->
<section class="intelligence-section">
  <div class="container">
    <h2 class="section-title">Code Intelligence</h2>
    <p class="section-sub">Sentrik understands your codebase &mdash; it scores quality, profiles your stack, and knows who should review what.</p>

    <div class="showcase-block">
      <div class="showcase-text">
        <h3>Quality Gradient Scoring</h3>
        <p>A 0&ndash;100 quality score across six dimensions: compliance, complexity, test coverage, documentation, consistency, and dependency health. Track trends over time and set minimum thresholds in your gate.</p>
      </div>
